---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="The editorial principles guiding accuracy, sourcing, corrections, and transparency at TechnoRaise.">
  <section class="prose-hero section-wrap">
    <span class="section-kicker">HOW WE WORK</span>
    <h1>Trust is built into the <em>process.</em></h1>
    <p class="prose-intro">Our editorial principles are designed to make technology coverage useful, fair, and accountable.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-layout section-wrap">
    <aside class="prose-aside"><span>EDITORIAL STANDARD</span><b>Accuracy before<br />attention.</b></aside>
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h2>Accuracy and verification</h2><p>Factual claims should be checked against reliable primary sources wherever practical. Technical explanations should be reviewed for clarity and correctness, and time-sensitive information should be dated and revisited when necessary.</p>
      <h2>Sources and attribution</h2><p>We aim to link to original documentation, research, official announcements, and other relevant sources. Quotes, data, images, and third-party material must be attributed and used with appropriate permission.</p>
      <h2>Analysis and opinion</h2><p>Analysis should be distinguishable from reported fact. Recommendations should explain their context and limitations rather than present personal preference as universal truth.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material errors should be corrected transparently. Once a monitored editorial contact address is published, readers will be able to use it to report potential errors.</p>
      <h2>AI-assisted work</h2><p>Tools may support research or editing, but they do not replace human responsibility for factual accuracy, originality, attribution, and final editorial review. AI-generated claims must not be treated as verified evidence.</p>
      <h2>Independence and disclosure</h2><p>Any material commercial relationship, sponsorship, or conflict of interest should be disclosed clearly. No such relationship is represented as existing by this policy page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>